          "text": "The pattern indexes as a body-centred tetragonal phase, with the systematic condition \\(h+k+l=2n\\). The best solution is **I4/mmm (No. 139)** with \\(a\\approx4.515\\) \u00c5, \\(c\\approx14.685\\) \u00c5, and \\(Z=2\\). It consists of alternating \\([\\mathrm{Cu_2S}]\\) and \\([\\mathrm{La_2O_2Se}]\\) layers. The principal peaks index as 002, 101, 004, 103, 110, 112, 105/006, 114, 200, and 211.\n\n```cif\ndata_La2Cu2SeSO2\n_audit_creation_method          'Structure solution from powder XRD'\n_chemical_name_common           'lanthanum copper selenide sulfide oxide'\n_chemical_formula_sum           'La2 Cu2 O2 S Se'\n_chemical_formula_structural    'La2Cu2SeSO2'\n_cell_formula_units_Z           2\n\n_cell_length_a                   4.5147(4)\n_cell_length_b                   4.5147(4)\n_cell_length_c                   14.6845(10)\n_cell_angle_alpha               90\n_cell_angle_beta                90\n_cell_angle_gamma               90\n_cell_volume                     299.3(1)\n\n_space_group_crystal_system     tetragonal\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt       'I 4/m m m'\n_space_group_IT_number          139\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type          'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength    1.5406\n\nloop_\n_atom_type_symbol\n_atom_type_oxidation_number\nLa  3\nCu  1\nO  -2\nS  -2\nSe -2\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nLa1 La 4 e 0.00000 0.00000 0.2945(15) 1.000 0.60\nCu1 Cu 4 c 0.00000 0.50000 0.00000     1.000 0.70\nO1  O  4 d 0.00000 0.50000 0.25000     1.000 0.80\nS1  S  2 a 0.00000 0.00000 0.00000     1.000 0.70\nSe1 Se 2 b 0.00000 0.00000 0.50000     1.000 0.70\n```\n\nThe lattice and space group are strongly constrained by the peak positions and absences. The La \\(z\\) coordinate is estimated from the powder intensities and should be regarded as approximate at the \\(10^{-3}\\) level; displacement parameters are nominal rather than independently refined. A setting with the 2a/2b labels interchanged and the origin shifted correspondingly is crystallographically equivalent, not a distinct alternative.",
